; A FIXED-LIMB BIGNUM WRITTEN IN OROBOROS, agreeing on all four targets.
;
; This is the rung ADR 0019's endpoint spelling exists to name: a FINITE range
; above the portable window gives a limb count, which gives a `build` of known
; length, which gives zero allocations. bigarith-2026-08-28 measured that form
; at 3.97x over `math/big`, 6.2x over `BigInteger` and 5.8x over `BigInt` -- and
; on the last two it is the ONLY way there, because those bignums are immutable.
;
; It is `examples/big/limbs.oro`, and what makes it interesting is that it names
; NO HOST: base-2^24 limbs, `/` and `%` for the carry split, and every operator
; the language's. Before integers.md promoted them this had to be written four
; times, once per spelling of `+`.
;
; inputs: 0 20 51
; expect: 0 7266130 2730071
;
; The expected values are limbs of 200! computed independently -- an ORACLE
; rather than a second implementation of ours, which is what `; expect:` is for
; (four backends can be wrong in the same way; a bug in the reader or the
; reducer is exactly the one a purely differential test cannot see).
;
; Limb 52 is 0 on purpose: 200! is about 1,245 bits, so 52 limbs are
; significant and the buffer is 64. A form that forgot to zero its tail would
; disagree there and nowhere else.
;
; AND IT IS FULLY PROVABLE -- 20 of 20 integer operations bounded, 12 of 12
; loops terminating, with no clamp and no declared range. Getting there needed
; two things the analysis did not have: a divisor CONTRACTS (a carry chain is
; `c' = (bounded + c) / 2^24`, which settles in two iterations and looks
; unbounded without it), and a loop variable holding a TABLE gets the join of
; its sources' element ranges (the accumulator is rebuilt every iteration, and
; reading it back was ⊤).
(def run (fn (k) (limb k)))

(def at (fn (t i) (if (< i 0) 0 (if (>= i (len t)) 0 (t i)))))

(def bn-of (fn (n v)
  (build n (fn (b)
    (loop ((b b) (i 0) (r v))
      (>= i n)  b
      else      (again (set b i (% r 16777216)) (+ i 1) (/ r 16777216)))))))

(def bn-mul-small (fn (n a k)
  (build n (fn (o)
    (loop ((o o) (i 0) (c 0))
      (>= i n)  o
      else      (let (+ (* (at a i) k) c) (fn (t)
                  (again (set o i (% t 16777216)) (+ i 1) (/ t 16777216)))))))))

(def bn-fact (fn (w n)
  (loop ((acc (bn-of w 1)) (i 2))
    (> i n)  acc
    else     (again (bn-mul-small w acc i) (+ i 1)))))

(def limb (fn (k) (at (bn-fact 64 200) k)))
